# App Review Information
app_review_information(
  demo_user: "demo@praticos.com.br",
  demo_password: "Demo@2024!",
  notes: <<~NOTES
    GUIDELINE 3.1.1 - PLEASE READ

    Company accounts are not created in the iOS app.
    - The iOS app has no business or organization registration. It is used by team members invited by their company and by owners of companies that already exist.
    - A signed-in user who is not linked to any company only sees a screen to join with an invite code from the company administrator, sign out or delete the account. The app does not mention or link to any other place to create a company.
    - The demo account (demo@praticos.com.br) is the owner of an existing company with sample data.

    In-App Purchase:
    - PraticOS is a freemium app. All paid plans are sold in the iOS app only through In-App Purchase.
    - The Free plan has monthly limits on photos, checklist form templates and team users. Paid plans raise these limits and remove the watermark from PDF work orders.
    - Paid plans are auto-renewable monthly subscriptions sold through In-App Purchase: Starter, Pro and Business (subscription group "PraticOS").
    - The app has no external purchase links or calls to action, and the website shows no prices.

    Where to find the paywall:
    1. Sign in with the demo account (steps below).
    2. Open the "Mais" (More) tab.
    3. In the "Assinatura" (Subscription) section, tap "Ver planos" (View plans).

    The paywall shows each plan with its price and period, the auto-renewal terms, Terms of Use, Privacy Policy and a Restore Purchases button. In the same section, "Gerenciar assinatura" (Manage subscription) opens subscription management and "Restaurar compras" (Restore purchases) restores previous purchases.

    PraticOS is a work-order management tool for service companies (mechanics, technicians, cleaning, etc.): work orders, customers, scheduling and teams. The payment features in work orders let a business record and charge its own customers for physical, real-world services performed outside the app (guideline 3.1.3(e)); they are not payments to PraticOS.

    ----------

    How to sign in with the demo account:

    1. On the login screen, tap the "Entrar com email" (Sign in with email) link below the social sign-in buttons.
    2. Enter the email and password provided.
    3. Tap "Entrar" (Sign in).

    The demo account owns an existing company with sample data:
    - 5 customers
    - 5 work orders in different statuses (quote, approved, in progress, completed)
    - Financial data on the dashboard

    All features of the app can be tested with this account.
  NOTES
)

